course: dictionary
lesson: 2581
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around the word, tells you which meaning is right. «The teacher gave a demonstration of how the magnet works.» Here demonstration means showing how something works, because the teacher is showing the magnet in action.
explain: «Hundreds of people held a peaceful demonstration outside the town hall.» Now demonstration means a public event where people gather or march to show what they think. Words like peaceful and outside the town hall are your clues. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the word shows a feeling or quality. «Her kind note was a demonstration of her love.» Nobody is showing how to do something here, and no one is marching. The word means a way of showing love. When a word fits more than one meaning, pick the one that matches the clues in the sentence.
fact: Demonstration means showing people how to do something or how something works.
fact: Demonstration can also mean a public event where people march or gather to show what they think.
fact: Demonstration can mean a way of showing a feeling or quality, as in «a demonstration of love».
fact: Useful phrases: give a demonstration, do a demonstration, a peaceful demonstration.
fact: «The crew gave a safety demonstration» means they showed passengers how to stay safe, so it is worth watching even if you have seen it before.
exercise: «The teacher gave a demonstration of how the magnet works.» What does demonstration mean here? | A crowd marching through town | *Showing how something works | A test you must pass | A kind of feeling
exercise: «Hundreds of people held a peaceful demonstration outside the town hall.» What does demonstration mean here? | A class trip | *A public event where people gather to show what they think | A sign saying stop | A lesson in drawing
exercise: «Her kind note was a demonstration of her love.» What does demonstration suggest? | A march through the streets | A lesson on how to write notes | A broken machine | *A way of showing a feeling
test: «The crew gave a safety demonstration before take-off.» What is a safety demonstration? | A loud noise | *Showing people what to do to stay safe | A public march | Showing how to fly the plane
test: «Monks give demonstrations of kung fu.» What does demonstrations mean in this sentence? | Prizes for the best students | *Shows of skill | Stories from long ago | Fights with no rules
exam: «You watch the safety demonstration even if you have seen it before, because each plane can be different.» Why do you watch it again? | Because it is a film | *Because each plane can be different | Because the crew are bored | Because it is a maths lesson
